From 7840bdc992175e01bb0b2a9766674c3a3ff7e983 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 16:44:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 53/62] fix(done): stop review-only close infinite loop
 (gfork-2cw)

Review-only work is not anchored to the worktree HEAD, but the done
close gate required the evidence comment's head_sha to equal the current
worktree HEAD. Every legitimate review-only close therefore failed
closed, the hook was never cleared, and the review polecat re-dispatched
forever.

- Drop the worktree-HEAD equality gate in hasFreshReviewEvidenceComment;
  keep the author + post-assignment-timestamp guards (and remove the now
  dead reviewEvidenceHeadSHA helper).
- Honor --skip-verify as an operator override that bypasses the
  review-only evidence gate for audit/test-only completion.
- On a review-only FATAL close skip, escalate (witness + mayor) and clear
  the hook instead of hard-returning, so a residual gate failure can no
  longer strand the hook and loop.

Update TestReviewOnlyCloseRejectsWrongAuthorOrHead -> WrongAuthor (head
gate dropped) and add tests for mismatched/missing head acceptance and
the --skip-verify bypass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
